BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sphera-media-lab-2026-open-call-discourse@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T111242Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: Sphera Media Lab 2026: Open Call for Masterclasses and Ke
 ynotes
DESCRIPTION:European Lab and the Sphera Network are opening submissions for
  the discourse programme of the next Sphera Media Lab\, the annual forum f
 or people defending independent media in Europe. THEMES: technological ind
 ependence (sovereignty\, tools\, mutualisation)\; economic independence (c
 ooperative models)\; editorial independence (press freedom\, resisting the
  far right). FORMATS SOUGHT: masterclasses\, led by an expert sharing adva
 nced knowledge\, technique and hands-on insight\; and keynotes\, inspiring
  talks grounded in a specific case study. WHO CAN PROPOSE: media outlets\,
  associations\, researchers and professionals. The organisers state they p
 ay particular attention to parity and diversity across their programmes an
 d ask that proposals take those criteria into account. WHAT IS COVERED: se
 lected contributors travel to Brussels with transport\, accommodation and 
 a fee covered. THE EVENT: Sphera Media Lab 2026 runs on 3 December 2026 at
  LaVallee in Brussels\, a full day of conferences\, masterclasses and work
 shops for independent media professionals from across Europe\, alongside t
 he premiere of a documentary on threats facing European journalists. APPLI
 CATION: submit your masterclass or keynote proposal via the Typeform at ar
 ty-farty.typeform.com/to/xnDikGGM before 31 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: 
 European Lab (Arty Farty) and the Sphera Network\, coordinated by Medianes
 \nLocation: LaVallee\, Rue Adolphe Lavallee 39\, 1080 Brussels\, Belgium. 
 Proposals are accepted regardless of where you are based\, but they should
  reflect a European perspective.\nAward: Selected contributors receive a f
 ee plus travel to Brussels and accommodation\, all covered by the organise
 rs. The fee amount is not published in the call. No submission fee.\nDurat
 ion: One-day event on 3 December 2026\; contributors deliver a single mast
 erclass or keynote\n\nMore: https://arty-farty.typeform.com/to/xnDikGGM?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://arty-farty.typeform.com/to/xnDikGGM?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:LaVallee\, Rue Adolphe Lavallee 39\, 1080 Brussels\, Belgium. Prop
 osals are accepted regardless of where you are based\, but they should ref
 lect a European perspective.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:american-academy-berlin-prize-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T111242Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260926
SUMMARY:Deadline: American Academy in Berlin: Berlin Prize Fellowship 2027-
 28
DESCRIPTION:The American Academy in Berlin is an independent\, nonprofit in
 stitute for advanced study in the arts\, humanities\, social sciences\, la
 w\, journalism and public policy\, whose primary mission is to strengthen 
 the cultural and intellectual ties between the United States and Germany. 
 Each year\, after a rigorous selection process\, the Academy awards roughl
 y two dozen semester-long Berlin Prize fellowships to individuals who demo
 nstrate excellence in their fields. DISCIPLINES: applications are welcome 
 across the humanities\, social sciences\, law\, journalism and various are
 as of public policy. The Academy generally encourages projects addressing 
 pressing issues of the day\, specifically naming democracy\, security\, te
 chnology and society (especially AI)\, energy including climate\, and glob
 al order. Dedicated fellowships also support projects in Jewish studies\, 
 German studies\, and public health and biotechnology. Project proposals ne
 ed not focus on Germany\, but candidates should explain how a residency in
  Berlin would enhance their work. NOT ACCEPTED: proposals in mathematics o
 r the natural sciences. NOTE FOR ARTISTS: visual artists and composers are
  invited through separate\, nomination-based competitions\, so there is no
  open application route for them here. ELIGIBILITY: fellowships are restri
 cted to citizens and permanent residents of the United States. Both emergi
 ng and established figures are eligible. PhD holders qualify as emerging s
 cholars with a strong record of peer-reviewed work beyond the dissertation
 \; candidates in non-academic fields such as journalism\, filmmaking and p
 olicy need a significant record of publication or production\; fiction and
  nonfiction writers must have published at least one book with a reputable
  press. WHAT FELLOWS DO: fellows present their work to audiences in and ar
 ound Berlin through lectures\, readings\, public discussions\, performance
 s and film screenings\, and should be willing to engage with relevant Germ
 an institutions\, organizations and the media\; these activities are integ
 ral to the Academy's mission of fostering transatlantic dialogue. APPLICAT
 ION MATERIALS: a project proposal of 1\,500 to 1\,750 words plus a one-pag
 e bibliography\; a curriculum vitae of up to 10 pages\; two writing sample
 s totalling no more than 60 pages\; and three letters of recommendation\, 
 which are due 2 October 2026. DEADLINE: Friday 25 September 2026 at 12:00 
 noon Eastern Time (18:00 Central European Time). TIMELINE: all candidates 
 are notified of the competition outcome by email in late March 2027\; the 
 2027-28 Berlin Prize recipients are announced in May 2027.\n\nOrganisation
 : American Academy in Berlin\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany\, at the Hans Arn
 hold Center. RESTRICTED: fellowships are open only to citizens and permane
 nt residents of the United States.\nAward: Monthly stipend of USD 5\,000\,
  plus roundtrip airfare\, accommodation at or near the Hans Arnhold Center
 \, partial board\, in-house library services and professional networking o
 pportunities. Roughly two dozen fellowships awarded each year. No applicat
 ion fee.\nDuration: One full academic semester (about 4 months). Fall runs
  mid-August to mid-December\; spring runs late January to late May.\n\nMor
 e: https://www.americanacademy.de/apply/apply-for-a-fellowship/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.americanacademy.de/apply/apply-for-a-fellowship/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany\, at the Hans Arnhold Center. RESTRICTED: fellows
 hips are open only to citizens and permanent residents of the United State
 s.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ditrapano-finch-manuscript-lab-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T111242Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260710
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260711
SUMMARY:Deadline: Giancarlo DiTrapano Foundation: The Finch Manuscript Lab 
 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Finch Manuscript Lab is a 2.5-month residency supporting wr
 iters completing book-length manuscripts\, hosted at the Finch Country Hou
 se in Serramezzana\, Italy\, and designed as the final sprint in the marat
 hon of writing a book. It offers living and work space\, writing time in a
  tranquil setting\, creative community\, and professional development incl
 uding manuscript consultations\, craft discussions\, and publishing semina
 rs. Residency dates: 1 October to 15 December 2026\; residents will be sel
 ected by 30 July 2026. FUNDING: thanks to the support of the Goethe Instit
 ute and Culture Moves Europe\, all selected residents receive a stipend of
  EUR 2\,280 for the residency period (EUR 30 per day in residence\, paid w
 eekly)\, a travel allowance of EUR 400 for distances under 5\,000 km from 
 Serramezzana or EUR 800 for distances over 5\,000 km\, an additional EUR 4
 00 for green travel (e.g. taking trains instead of planes)\, and additiona
 l support of EUR 200 for parents of children under 18. ELIGIBILITY: applic
 ants must be over 18 and a legal resident of one of the 39 Culture Moves E
 urope eligible countries\, excluding Italy\; this includes all EU member s
 tates other than Italy and 13 participating non-EU countries (Albania\, An
 dorra\, Armenia\, Bosnia and Herzegovina\, Georgia\, Iceland\, Kosovo\, Mo
 ldova\, Montenegro\, North Macedonia\, Norway\, Serbia\, and Tunisia). APP
 LICATION (via Submittable\, in order of importance): a short sample of pas
 t work (any length\, though only the first 30 pages may be read)\; a brief
  note\, up to one page\, explaining the manuscript or book project to be w
 orked on in residency\, where you are in the creation process\, and why yo
 u are interested\; an excerpt of the book project not exceeding 30 pages (
 prose\, poetry\, mixed media\, photography\, or any other form of artist's
  book is acceptable)\; and a CV in English. NOTE ON DEADLINE: the foundati
 on's text gives the open call as 15 June to 10 July 2026\, while the Submi
 ttable page lists a close of Wednesday 15 July 2026 at 12:00 PM\; apply by
  10 July to be safe.\n\nOrganisation: The Giancarlo DiTrapano Foundation f
 or Literature and the Arts\nLocation: Finch Country House\, Serramezzana\,
  Italy\; open to legal residents of the 39 Culture Moves Europe eligible c
 ountries\, excluding Italy\nAward: EUR 2\,280 stipend for the residency pe
 riod (EUR 30 per day in residence\, paid weekly)\, plus travel allowance o
 f EUR 400 (under 5\,000 km) or EUR 800 (over 5\,000 km)\, an additional EU
 R 400 green-travel top-up (e.g. trains instead of planes)\, and EUR 200 ad
 ditional support for parents of children under 18. Supported by the Goethe
  Institute and Culture Moves Europe.\nDuration: 2.5 months\, 1 October to 
 15 December 2026\n\nMore: https://ditrapanofoundation.submittable.com/subm
 it/171cc54d-b582-47a3-93a4-47c46b65904b/the-finch-manuscript-lab?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ditrapanofoundation.submittable.com/submit/171cc54d-b582-47a3-9
 3a4-47c46b65904b/the-finch-manuscript-lab?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Finch Country House\, Serramezzana\, Italy\; open to legal residen
 ts of the 39 Culture Moves Europe eligible countries\, excluding Italy
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:page-not-found-neu-commission-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T111242Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: NEU Commission 2026
DESCRIPTION:Page Not Found announces the third edition of the NEU Commissio
 n\, which intends to support the emergence of alternative voices within co
 ntemporary art. It targets a group currently under-represented in Europe: 
 art students with limited financial means who are required to provide a gu
 arantee for their visa and to pay high non-EU tuition fees\, economical ba
 rriers to their participation in art and knowledge production in The Nethe
 rlands. Page Not Found will commission three art students from non-Europea
 n countries to each write an essay or a free-form text in English. Each se
 lected writer receives EUR 2\,000 for the commission\, provided as an adva
 nce payment in September 2026\; the commissioned texts are published at a 
 later date. OPEN CALL: only students enrolled in Dutch art academies who a
 re NOT nationals of the European Economic Area are eligible. The commissio
 ned text does not need to be submitted when answering the open call\; the 
 jury selects recipients based on their previous writing and financial need
 . Review the Rules of the Open Call and the FAQ before applying. Deadline:
  Friday 31 July 2026\, 23:59 CEST (Amsterdam).\n\nOrganisation: Page Not F
 ound\nLocation: The Netherlands\; open to non-EEA-national students enroll
 ed at Dutch art academies.\nAward: EUR 2\,000 each to three commissioned w
 riters\, paid as an advance in September 2026.\nDuration: One-time commiss
 ion\; commissioned texts published at a later date\n\nMore: http://neu-com
 mission.page-not-found.nl/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
URL:http://neu-commission.page-not-found.nl/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Netherlands\; open to non-EEA-national students enrolled at Du
 tch art academies.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:translation-house-looren-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T111242Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Translation House Looren: Translators' Residencies and Pr
 o Helvetia Stipends 2027
DESCRIPTION:Translators' residency at Uebersetzerhaus Looren in Wernetshaus
 en near Zurich. Looren offers a free residency for literary translators wi
 th a current contract\, including six competitive CHF 4\,000 stipend grant
 s per year tied to one-month residencies. The Pro Helvetia residency progr
 amme (separately funded) has a 2026-10-15 deadline for 2027 stays. The Jam
 es Joyce Scholarship and Looren Residency 2027 closes 2026-10-31. General 
 free residencies are accepted on a rolling basis throughout the year. ELIG
 IBILITY: literary translators with substantial published work and a curren
 t translation contract\; any language combination is welcome. Apply via th
 e application page on looren.net. No application fee.\n\nOrganisation: Ueb
 ersetzerhaus Looren\nLocation: Wernetshausen\, Switzerland (Zurich region)
 \nAward: Free residency stay (apartments at the translation house). Six co
 mpetitive CHF 4\,000 translation grants per year\, each tied to a one-mont
 h residency. Pro Helvetia residency programme separately funded. James Joy
 ce Scholarship and Looren Residency 2027 has its own conditions. No applic
 ation fee.\nDuration: Stays of typically 2 weeks to 2 months\; CHF 4\,000 
 stipend grants tied to one-month residencies\n\nMore: https://looren.net/e
 n/residencies/application-for-a-stay?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://looren.net/en/residencies/application-for-a-stay?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Wernetshausen\, Switzerland (Zurich region)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:letterenfonds-project-grants-translators@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T111242Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Nederlands Letterenfonds: Project Grants for Literary Tra
 nslators (August 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Project subsidies from the Nederlands Letterenfonds for advance
 d literary translators with a current publishing contract for a translatio
 n from or into Dutch. The next round closes 15 August 2026\; decisions are
  made approximately four months after the deadline (December). ELIGIBILITY
 : literary translators with a substantial published portfolio and a contra
 cted translation project\; primary income must be below EUR 52\,500.\n\nOr
 ganisation: Nederlands Letterenfonds (Dutch Foundation for Literature)\nLo
 cation: Worldwide (literary translators with a contracted translation from
  or into Dutch)\nAward: Project-based subsidy. Income cap EUR 52\,500 for 
 primary income. Standard minimum rates: EUR 0.0802/word for prose\; EUR 2.
 92/line for poetry. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\, scaled 
 to the contracted translation\n\nMore: https://www.letterenfonds.nl/en-car
 ibbean/funding/project-grants-for-literary-translators?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.letterenfonds.nl/en-caribbean/funding/project-grants-for-li
 terary-translators?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
LOCATION:Worldwide (literary translators with a contracted translation from
  or into Dutch)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jan-michalski-foundation-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T111242Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: Jan Michalski Foundation: Writers Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Residency for writers and translators at the Jan Michalski Foun
 dation in Montricher\, Switzerland\, set in seven distinctive 'cabin' modu
 les hanging from an openwork canopy\, offering conditions to start\, conti
 nue or finish a writing project. Around forty authors from around the worl
 d (emerging to established) are hosted each year. Open to all kinds of wri
 ting and all languages\, with priority given to literary writers and trans
 lators\; other disciplines are welcome as long as literature is at the hea
 rt of the project. Residencies are for individuals or pairs working on a c
 ommon project (e.g. a writer and a translator). A percentage of residencie
 s are dedicated to nature writing. WHAT IS PROVIDED: a private cabin for i
 ndependent living (a separate cabin per person for pairs\; one accessible 
 cabin for reduced mobility)\, travel costs to and from home\, a weekly all
 owance of CHF 400\, breakfast and lunch\, electric bikes\, and daytime lib
 rary access. ELIGIBILITY: no age or nationality restrictions\; beginners a
 ccepted\; one application per year\; former residents may not reapply (fam
 ilies\, children and pets cannot be accommodated). Stays cannot be split i
 nto multiple periods. Selection is by a panel chaired by Vera Michalski-Ho
 ffmann\, assessing the literary quality of the project\, the candidate's b
 ackground\, and whether the stay length matches the project scope. APPLICA
 TION: online in English or French (work excerpts may be in any language)\;
  the 2027 form is open 2 June to 31 August 2026\; selected candidates anno
 unced December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Jan Michalski Foundation for Writing
  and Literature\nLocation: Montricher\, Switzerland (Swiss Jura\, near Lau
 sanne and Geneva)\nAward: Weekly allowance of CHF 400\, plus travel costs 
 to and from home covered\, accommodation in a private cabin\, and breakfas
 t and lunch provided. Electric bikes and library access included.\nDuratio
 n: Two weeks to three months (first 2027 residents arrive mid-January 2027
 )\n\nMore: https://fondation-janmichalski.com/en/residences?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fondation-janmichalski.com/en/residences?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Montricher\, Switzerland (Swiss Jura\, near Lausanne and Geneva)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
